        To accurately forecast international payroll budgets, finance directors must calculate the Total Cost to Company (TCTC). The formal mathematical relationship governing total monthly employer expenditure per distributed team member is expressed as:
      </p>

      <pre is:raw class="bg-slate-950 p-4 rounded-lg border border-slate-800 text-xs font-mono text-amber-300 overflow-x-auto"><code>TCTC = Base_SaaS_Fee + (Net_Salary_Local * (1 + Employer_Tax_Rate) / Spot_Rate) * (1 + Spread_Markup) + Deposit_Opportunity_Cost
</code></pre>

      <p>
        Where:
      </p>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-slate-300 list-disc pl-5">
        <li><strong>Base_SaaS_Fee</strong> is the fixed platform fee ($599/mo).</li>
        <li><strong>Employer_Tax_Rate</strong> represents mandatory statutory employer contributions (e.g. 20.48% ZUS in Poland, 28% in France).</li>
        <li><strong>Spot_Rate</strong> is the real-time interbank mid-market exchange rate ($USD \to Local$).</li>
        <li><strong>Spread_Markup</strong> is the asymmetric platform spread (&Delta;<sub>FX</sub> = 0.0165 to 0.0240).</li>
        <li><strong>Deposit_Opportunity_Cost</strong> represents the capital yield lost on the mandatory 1-month or 2-month security deposit locked in non-interest-bearing escrow accounts.</li>
      </ul>

