      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white border-b border-slate-800 pb-2">
        Frequently Asked Questions: EOR Currency Conversions &amp; International Payroll Fees
      </h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 my-6">
        <div class="border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-4 bg-slate-900/40">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-white mb-2">How do EOR platforms make money on FX currency conversion?</h3>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
            In addition to their advertised monthly software fee (e.g. $599/mo), platforms apply an undisclosed 1.5% to 2.8% spread markup over the real interbank mid-market exchange rate when converting employer funds (USD) to local currency payroll (EUR, PLN, BRL).
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-4 bg-slate-900/40">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-white mb-2">Which platform has lower FX markups: Remote.com or Deel?</h3>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
            Our empirical transaction audit revealed Remote.com averages a 1.65% FX spread markup, whereas Deel averages 2.15% on standard accounts, although Deel offers negotiated flat-fee FX tiers for enterprise contracts exceeding $1M annual volume.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-4 bg-slate-900/40">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-white mb-2">How can employers eliminate FX conversion markups completely?</h3>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
            Employers can fund their billing balances directly in the local payout currency (e.g. holding EUR or GBP in multi-currency accounts like Wise Business or Airwallex) to bypass the EOR's internal conversion engine.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-4 bg-slate-900/40">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-white mb-2">What is an FX volatility reserve in international payroll?</h3>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
            An FX volatility reserve is a mandatory buffer deposit (typically 1.5% to 5% of gross payroll) collected by EORs in high-volatility countries to guarantee local statutory tax and social security remittances if currency markets fluctuate before state deadlines.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

